    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the area of the square, we need to first determine the length of its side. According to the problem, the length of the side of the square can be expressed in two different ways: \\(4x - 15\\) meters and \\(20 - 3x\\) meters. Since both expressions represent the same length, we can set them equal to each other and solve for \\(x\\):\n\n\\[\n4x - 15 = 20 - 3x\n\\]\n\nNext, we will solve this equation for \\(x\\):\n\n1. Add \\(3x\\) to both sides of the equation:\n\\[\n4x + 3x - 15 = 20\n\\]\n\\[\n7x - 15 = 20\n\\]\n\n2. Add 15 to both sides of the equation:\n\\[\n7x = 35\n\\]\n\n3. Divide both sides by 7:\n\\[\nx = 5\n\\]\n\nNow that we have the value of \\(x\\), we can substitute it back into either expression for the side length to find the actual length of the side of the square. Let's use \\(4x - 15\\):\n\n\\[\n4x - 15 = 4(5) - 15 = 20 - 15 = 5 \\text{ meters}\n\\]\n\nThe length of the side of the square is 5 meters. The area of a square is given by the square of the side length:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = (\\text{side length})^2 = 5^2 = 25 \\text{ square meters}\n\\]\n\nThus, the area of the square is \\(\\boxed{25}\\) square meters.",
