    "text": "To find the area of the square, we need to determine the length of one of its sides. We are given two expressions for the length of the side: \\(4x - 15\\) meters and \\(20 - 3x\\) meters. Since both expressions represent the same length, we can set them equal to each other and solve for \\(x\\).\n\n\\[\n4x - 15 = 20 - 3x\n\\]\n\nFirst, we will add \\(3x\\) to both sides of the equation to combine the \\(x\\) terms on one side:\n\n\\[\n4x + 3x - 15 = 20\n\\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n7x - 15 = 20\n\\]\n\nNext, we will add 15 to both sides to isolate the term with \\(x\\):\n\n\\[\n7x = 35\n\\]\n\nNow, we will divide both sides by 7 to solve for \\(x\\):\n\n\\[\nx = 5\n\\]\n\nWith \\(x\\) found, we can substitute \\(x = 5\\) back into either expression for the side length to find the actual length of the side. We will use \\(4x - 15\\):\n\n\\[\n4(5) - 15 = 20 - 15 = 5 \\text{ meters}\n\\]\n\nThe side length of the square is 5 meters. The area \\(A\\) of a square is given by the formula:\n\n\\[\nA = \\text{side length}^2\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the side length we found:\n\n\\[\nA = 5^2 = 25 \\text{ square meters}\n\\]\n\nThus, the area of the square is \\(\\boxed{25}\\) square meters.",
